cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Chokepoint: a typed-alert tower-defense for learning Python"
message: "If you use, fork, or build on this project, please cite it and keep the attribution."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "joshualytle"
    website: "https://github.com/joshualytle"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshualytle/Chokepoint"
url: "https://github.com/joshualytle/Chokepoint"
abstract: >-
  Chokepoint is a typed-alert tower-defense game that teaches the skills behind
  high-volume alert pipelines — typed routing, consumer specialization and
  coverage, queue/latency backpressure, and flood/burst handling — as a game.
  It ships a desktop (pygame) build and a native-web build (Pyodide + HTML/canvas)
  where the same pure Python core runs in the browser and the player writes
  Python to hold the line.
keywords:
  - tower-defense
  - learning-python
  - alert-pipeline
  - education
  - pygame
  - pyodide
license: MIT
